 "brief_text": "We run a regional electrical wholesaler and deliver directly to trade customers. Our goal is to cut the delivery bill by £60,000 over the coming year while keeping customers confident about when their orders will arrive. We currently spend £420,000 a year on delivery and achieve 96% on-time arrivals. Our options are Keep separate routes and Merge routes. Merge routes combines the quieter afternoon rounds, reducing delivery spending by about £75,000 a year. It needs £12,000 upfront for scheduling work and driver training. We expect on-time arrivals to fall by about one percentage point because longer rounds leave less room for delays. Keep separate routes should maintain current costs and performance. Customers often need parts for jobs already in progress, so a late van can hold up their work. The team thinks the quieter rounds are an obvious place to save, but branch managers worry about complaints and extra chasing.",
